Summary
-------

  This README file describes how the .bif and .sim formatted vector files
are generate from the BusTalk verification code. 

  This file also indicates which testbench should be used with each
test case.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Building the verification code
------------------------------

  The verification BusTalk code is built using the verification/bustest 
makefile. This will generate .bif and a .sim files in the 
verification/bustest/invec directory. 

eg : To build the POResetTest
> make POResetTest

Note: Please refer to the 'makefile' for legal 'testname's.

Note: The files generated in the invec directory are:
bif0.sim    : Verilog testbench AHB0 stimulus.
bif1.sim    : Verilog testbench AHB1 stimulus.
bif2.sim    : Verilog testbench AHB2 stimulus.
bif3.sim    : Verilog testbench AHB3 stimulus.
infile0.bif : VHDL testbench AHB0 stimulus.
infile1.bif : VHDL testbench AHB1 stimulus.
infile2.bif : VHDL testbench AHB2 stimulus.
infile3.bif : VHDL testbench AHB3 stimulus.

Note: The make "all" option should not be used. This option will not compile
all the tests. An error message is flagged if a make "all" is attempted.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Running a simulation
--------------------

  The verification code makes use of 14 testbenches (tbench and
tbench1 to tbench13). This allows the MPMC to be tested with a large
number of different memory device configurations.

  The verification tests are required to be executed an appropriate 
testbench. A list of which tests should be executed on which testbench
can be found in the section below.

To run the simulation using modelsim, from the verification/vhdl or the
verification/verilog directory type,
"make -f SimMakefile_modelsim.mk TBENCH=<testbench_number> rtl"
 
eg : To run a simulation using tbench7
> make -f SimMakefile_modelsim.mk TBENCH=7 rtl

eg : To run a simulation using tbench
> make -f SimMakefile_modelsim.mk TBENCH= rtl

To run the simulation using Verilog-XL, from the verification/verilog
directory type, 
"make -f SimMakefile_LDV.mk TBENCH=<testbench_number> rtl"

eg : To run a simulation using tbench5
> make -f SimMakefile_LDV.mk TBENCH=5 rtl

eg : To run a simulation using tbench
> make -f SimMakefile_LDV.mk TBENCH= rtl

